  "branch": "bugfix/r3.12-zstd-frame-checksums-20261111",
  "head": "4064429ecfaaeb01e67720f30d698ce7c08e7189",
  "topic": "验证每个 Zstandard 帧的内容校验和，拒绝损坏数据和损坏的后续拼接帧",
  "title": "Verify Zstandard content checksums before returning recovered bytes (R3.12)",
  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe existing Zstandard loop reads each frame through `ruzstd::StreamingDecoder`, but that decoder leaves verification of the optional content checksum to its caller. A frame with a changed raw payload or checksum can therefore return recovered data successfully. A later damaged frame in a concatenated stream is also accepted.\n\n## Change\n\nEnable the existing `ruzstd` checksum-calculation feature and compare every present checksum after that frame's output has been fully read. A mismatch returns `DecompressError::Corrupt` before any recovered result is returned.\n\nThe reader retains checksum-free frames, skippable frames, concatenation and one output budget for the entire stream. A budget stop still reports `TooLarge`. The check also applies when Zstandard is used inside a ZIP entry, even if that entry's outer CRC agrees with its uncompressed bytes.\n\nThe `ruzstd` version remains 0.9.1. Enabling its `hash` feature adds only the pure-Rust `twox-hash` 2.1.5 package; existing package versions are unchanged. The lockfile was generated by Cargo, then checked byte-for-byte in validation.\n\nThe independent R3.12 claim was published before implementation at `3f13bd90`. It was replayed at `810452ca` on main `86d047cbc5368ca595c83e045893fb39c7f3f7f8`. Final head: `4064429ecfaaeb01e67720f30d698ce7c08e7189`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- [Unchanged-main negative control](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43056722259/job/130648018637): **4 regression groups fail and 3 controls pass**. The four failures cover corrupted checksum bytes, changed raw payload, bad concatenated frames and a ZIP member with a valid outer CRC but a corrupt inner checksum.\n- [Complete fixed validation and native comparison](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43057798485/job/130651839037): **1710 passed, 0 failed, 10 existing ignored, 208 test targets**. All seven new groups pass.\n- The same native producer, Python **3.14.0** with libzstd **1.5.5**, supplies **59 cases** to the actual public Rust decoder. They include empty, ASCII, Unicode, compressed and 502,144-byte multi-block outputs; checksum-free frames; each checksum byte; truncated trailers; output limits; skippable frames; and corruption in first, later or empty concatenated frames. The original decoder wrongly accepts **24 corruptions**. The correction agrees with the native results on **all 59**, comparing complete output bytes.\n- [Final current-main integration](https://github.com/Afloat16/billion-context/actions/runs/43059804924/job/130658941218): **1712 passed, 0 failed, 10 existing ignored, 208 test targets**, including the intervening upstream code-signature changes. The four product, test and dependency files are identical to the fully validated implementation; all other upstream file blobs and modes are preserved. The PR changes only six files, including its ROADMAP and STATUS entries.\n- Formatting, strict all-target formats Clippy, layer and lock checks, secret scanning, all five L0–L2 WebAssembly builds, and clean-tree checks pass at the final head with Rust **1.99.0**.\n\nThe first fixed validation stopped at formatting of two fixture arrays. Those arrays were formatted without changing their values or product code; the complete successful runs above retain the original assertions. The initial native preparation also verified the precise Cargo dependency change.\n\n## Related work\n\nChecked #1340, which adds concatenated Zstandard frames, and #1371, which checks gzip header CRCs. This change verifies the optional Zstandard content checksum after each already-supported frame. Existing ZIP identity/framing work in #1138 is unchanged.\n\nThe reference producer's checksum behavior is documented in [Python's Zstandard API](https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/compression.zstd.html). The dependency's checksum API was checked against its fixed 0.9.1 source before enabling it.\n",
  "url": "https://github.com/storytold/craft-anything/compare/main...Afloat16:bugfix/r3.12-zstd-frame-checksums-20261111?expand=1&title=Verify%20Zstandard%20content%20checksums%20before%20returning%20recovered%20bytes%20(R3.12)&body=%23%23%20Problem%0A%0AThe%20existing%20Zstandard%20loop%20reads%20each%20frame%20through%20%60ruzstd%3A%3AStreamingDecoder%60%2C%20but%20that%20decoder%20leaves%20verification%20of%20the%20optional%20content%20checksum%20to%20its%20caller.%20A%20frame%20with%20a%20changed%20raw%20payload%20or%20checksum%20can%20therefore%20return%20recovered%20data%20successfully.%20A%20later%20damaged%20frame%20in%20a%20concatenated%20stream%20is%20also%20accepted.%0A%0A%23%23%20Change%0A%0AEnable%20the%20existing%20%60ruzstd%60%20checksum-calculation%20feature%20and%20compare%20every%20present%20checksum%20after%20that%20frame's%20output%20has%20been%20fully%20read.%20A%20mismatch%20returns%20%60DecompressError%3A%3ACorrupt%60%20before%20any%20recovered%20result%20is%20returned.%0A%0AThe%20reader%20retains%20checksum-free%20frames%2C%20skippable%20frames%2C%20concatenation%20and%20one%20output%20budget%20for%20the%20entire%20stream.%20A%20budget%20stop%20still%20reports%20%60TooLarge%60.%20The%20check%20also%20applies%20when%20Zstandard%20is%20used%20inside%20a%20ZIP%20entry%2C%20even%20if%20that%20entry's%20outer%20CRC%20agrees%20with%20its%20uncompressed%20bytes.%0A%0AThe%20%60ruzstd%60%20version%20remains%200.9.1.%20Enabling%20its%20%60hash%60%20feature%20adds%20only%20the%20pure-Rust%20%60twox-hash%60%202.1.5%20package%3B%20existing%20package%20versions%20are%20unchanged.%20The%20lockfile%20was%20generated%20by%20Cargo%2C%20then%20checked%20byte-for-byte%20in%20validation.%0A%0AThe%20independent%20R3.12%20claim%20was%20published%20before%20implementation%20at%20%603f13bd90%60.%20It%20was%20replayed%20at%20%60810452ca%60%20on%20main%20%6086d047cbc5368ca595c83e045893fb39c7f3f7f8%60.%20Final%20head%3A%20%604064429ecfaaeb01e67720f30d698ce7c08e7189%60.%0A%0A%23%23%20Validation%0A%0A-%20%5BUnchanged-main%20negative%20control%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fbillion-context%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43056722259%2Fjob%2F130648018637)%3A%20**4%20regression%20groups%20fail%20and%203%20controls%20pass**.%20The%20four%20failures%20cover%20corrupted%20checksum%20bytes%2C%20changed%20raw%20payload%2C%20bad%20concatenated%20frames%20and%20a%20ZIP%20member%20with%20a%20valid%20outer%20CRC%20but%20a%20corrupt%20inner%20checksum.%0A-%20%5BComplete%20fixed%20validation%20and%20native%20comparison%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fbillion-context%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43057798485%2Fjob%2F130651839037)%3A%20**1710%20passed%2C%200%20failed%2C%2010%20existing%20ignored%2C%20208%20test%20targets**.%20All%20seven%20new%20groups%20pass.%0A-%20The%20same%20native%20producer%2C%20Python%20**3.14.0**%20with%20libzstd%20**1.5.5**%2C%20supplies%20**59%20cases**%20to%20the%20actual%20public%20Rust%20decoder.%20They%20include%20empty%2C%20ASCII%2C%20Unicode%2C%20compressed%20and%20502%2C144-byte%20multi-block%20outputs%3B%20checksum-free%20frames%3B%20each%20checksum%20byte%3B%20truncated%20trailers%3B%20output%20limits%3B%20skippable%20frames%3B%20and%20corruption%20in%20first%2C%20later%20or%20empty%20concatenated%20frames.%20The%20original%20decoder%20wrongly%20accepts%20**24%20corruptions**.%20The%20correction%20agrees%20with%20the%20native%20results%20on%20**all%2059**%2C%20comparing%20complete%20output%20bytes.%0A-%20%5BFinal%20current-main%20integration%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fbillion-context%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43059804924%2Fjob%2F130658941218)%3A%20**1712%20passed%2C%200%20failed%2C%2010%20existing%20ignored%2C%20208%20test%20targets**%2C%20including%20the%20intervening%20upstream%20code-signature%20changes.%20The%20four%20product%2C%20test%20and%20dependency%20files%20are%20identical%20to%20the%20fully%20validated%20implementation%3B%20all%20other%20upstream%20file%20blobs%20and%20modes%20are%20preserved.%20The%20PR%20changes%20only%20six%20files%2C%20including%20its%20ROADMAP%20and%20STATUS%20entries.%0A-%20Formatting%2C%20strict%20all-target%20formats%20Clippy%2C%20layer%20and%20lock%20checks%2C%20secret%20scanning%2C%20all%20five%20L0%E2%80%93L2%20WebAssembly%20builds%2C%20and%20clean-tree%20checks%20pass%20at%20the%20final%20head%20with%20Rust%20**1.99.0**.%0A%0AThe%20first%20fixed%20validation%20stopped%20at%20formatting%20of%20two%20fixture%20arrays.%20Those%20arrays%20were%20formatted%20without%20changing%20their%20values%20or%20product%20code%3B%20the%20complete%20successful%20runs%20above%20retain%20the%20original%20assertions.%20The%20initial%20native%20preparation%20also%20verified%20the%20precise%20Cargo%20dependency%20change.%0A%0A%23%23%20Related%20work%0A%0AChecked%20%231340%2C%20which%20adds%20concatenated%20Zstandard%20frames%2C%20and%20%231371%2C%20which%20checks%20gzip%20header%20CRCs.%20This%20change%20verifies%20the%20optional%20Zstandard%20content%20checksum%20after%20each%20already-supported%20frame.%20Existing%20ZIP%20identity%2Fframing%20work%20in%20%231138%20is%20unchanged.%0A%0AThe%20reference%20producer's%20checksum%20behavior%20is%20documented%20in%20%5BPython's%20Zstandard%20API%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.python.org%2F3.14%2Flibrary%2Fcompression.zstd.html).%20The%20dependency's%20checksum%20API%20was%20checked%20against%20its%20fixed%200.9.1%20source%20before%20enabling%20it.%0A",
